    "body": "<p><strong><a href=\"https://github.com/muruhq/muru\">Muru</a></strong></p> Graham Dumpleton started <a href=\"https://modwsgi.readthedocs.io/\">mod_wsgi</a> 20 years ago, and has been thinking about the ideal way to serve Python web applications in production ever since.</p> <p>Muru is his new, AI-assisted Rust server that aims to provide the best possible tools for running ASGI and WSGI Python apps both in development and production.</p> <p>As <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Sep/11/wrapture/\">he did with wrapture</a>, he's been publishing an extraordinarily detailed account of the project as he works on it - as part of his development process.</p> <p>Here's everything he's published so far, all in the last three weeks:</p> <ul> <li>2026-11-04 — <a href=\"https://grahamdumpleton.me/pos",
