    "id": "builder_blog:builder_blog:https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/20/llm-gemini/",
    "source": "builder_blog",
    "sourceItemId": "builder_blog:https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/20/llm-gemini/",
    "title": "llm-gemini 0.38.1",
    "summary": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/llm-gemini/releases/tag/0.38.1\">llm-gemini 0.38.1</a></p> <p>Gemini 4 Carbon only supports <code>low</code>, <code>medium</code> and <code>high</code> reasoning levels - but Gemini 4 Hydrogen and Gemini 4 Neon both have an extra <code>xhigh</code> level.</p> <p>I missed that when I added those models to the <code>llm-gemini</code> plugin, which is now fixed in this dot release.</p> <p>The <code>xhigh</code> setting for Hydrogen make",
    "body": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/llm-gemini/releases/tag/0.38.1\">llm-gemini 0.38.1</a></p> <p>Gemini 4 Carbon only supports <code>low</code>, <code>medium</code> and <code>high</code> reasoning levels - but Gemini 4 Hydrogen and Gemini 4 Neon both have an extra <code>xhigh</code> level.</p> <p>I missed that when I added those models to the <code>llm-gemini</code> plugin, which is now fixed in this dot release.</p> <p>The <code>xhigh</code> setting for Hydrogen makes a <em>significant</em> difference. I updated my <a href=\"https://static.simonwillison.net/static/2026/gemini-4-carbon-neon-hydrogen-with-xhigh.html\">Gemini 4 comparison grid</a> - note how Hydrogen at high used 5,311 output tokens and cost 3.99 cents, but the same model at xhigh used 31,477 output",
    "url": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/20/llm-gemini/",
    "sourceName": "Simon Willison",
    "sourceCategory": "technical",
    "authorName": "Simon Willison",
